<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 34,080 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 34,080 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 34,080 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday, compared to 44,675 tonnes on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Thursday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			6,148	     9,051</p>
<p>    Import cargo			27,932	    35,624</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships are expected to sail and five to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Sulpher		 3,531	  Saleem Three	    due</p>
<p>Fuel oil		30,000	 Ying Song Hu	    30/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil		26,000	 Zoras		     due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
